target: internal/report/report.go
verify: go test ./internal/report/ -count=1 -run 'TestParityWithPrReport/a_roster_findings_count_that_is_an_empty_list_with_a_space'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    the empty-container case was matched by exact spelling, defended by a comment claiming json.RawMessage can hold no internal whitespace because "encoding/json emits none in one it wrote". A RawMessage is populated by Unmarshal COPYING the input subslice, not written by encoding/json: measured, `{"findings": [ ], "status": {\t}}` decodes to `"[ ]"` and `"{\t}"`, and TrimSpace only strips the outside. So one space from a hand-edited store walked past the match and rendered "[ ]" into the PR comment where the oracle renders nothing — the same presence divergence the case was added to close, one spelling over, and invisible to the three fixtures that all used the compact form runlog.py writes. Compacting first makes the switch a test of the value, which is what the zero-number case below it was already fixed to be.
